📌 Step 1: Install CSI Snapshot CRDs (if not already installed)
Kubernetes needs the CSI snapshot feature enabled. Run the following to check if the necessary CRDs are installed:
kubectl get volumesnapshotclasses

If no results appear, install the CSI Snapshot CRDs:
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes-csi/external-snapshotter/release-6.2/client/config/crd/snapshot.storage.k8s.io_volumesnapshots.yaml
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes-csi/external-snapshotter/release-6.2/client/config/crd/snapshot.storage.k8s.io_volumesnapshotclasses.yaml
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes-csi/external-snapshotter/release-6.2/client/config/crd/snapshot.storage.k8s.io_volumesnapshotcontents.yaml

Verify the CRDs are installed:
kubectl get crds | grep snapshot


📌 Step 2: Set Up a CSI VolumeSnapshotClass for NFS
Now, create a CSI VolumeSnapshotClass to define snapshot behavior for your NFS StorageClass.
Create a file csi-nfs-snapshotclass.yaml:

apiVersion: snapshot.storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: VolumeSnapshotClass
metadata:
  name: csi-nfs-snapshotclass
driver: nfs.csi.k8s.io
deletionPolicy: Delete

Apply the file:
kubectl apply -f csi-nfs-snapshotclass.yaml

Now, check if it's properly created:
kubectl get volumesnapshotclass

Expected output:
NAME                     DRIVER           DELETIONPOLICY
csi-nfs-snapshotclass    nfs.csi.k8s.io   Delete